==Trivia==
*In the Turkish, Korean, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Lumberjack's name translates to "Woodcutter". In the Chinese and Finnish language settings of the game, the Lumberjack's name translates to "Crazy Woodcutter" and "Logman" respectively.
*The Lumberjack's Evolution is 1 of 5 [[cards]] that has had its [[Card Evolution|Cycles]] required changed, the others being [[Bomber/Evolution|Bomber]], [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]], [[Ice Spirit/Evolution|Ice Spirit]], and [[Baby Dragon/Evolution|Baby Dragon]].
*In the card's description, the "''Who you gonna call?''" line combined with him turning into a ghost upon death is a reference to Ghostbusters.
*When attacking, the Lumberjack will say "''Chop chop!''" or “''Timber!''”. He also laughs when deployed and when the Lumberjack Ghost surges.
**Along with the [[Knight/Evolution|Knight]] and [[Barbarians/Evolution|Barbarians]], he is voice acted by [https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1423395/ John Mondelli].
**The Lumberjack is 1 of 9 evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Bomber, [[Wizard/Evolution|Wizard]], [[Goblin Cage/Evolution|Goblin Brawler]], [[Witch/Evolution|Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A./Evolution|P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Hunter/Evolution|Hunter]], [[Executioner/Evolution|Executioner]], and [[Mega Knight/Evolution|Mega Knight]].
*Before the Lumberjack Evolution's release, the Lumberjack Ghost's damage was decreased by 33%.
